      "errorMessage": "<task id=\"ses_f0683906cffegRDM9yPn2EOn4V\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nI have gathered a complete picture. Here is the thorough research report.\n\n---\n\n# Server-side notification / Inbox primitives — research report for US-156\n\n## 1. The notification module\n\nRoot: `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/notification/`\n\n### 1.1 Full file listing\n\n```\nconstants/\n  notification-channel.constant.ts        NOTIFICATION_CHANNELS = INBOX | EMAIL | NONE\n  notification-event-name.constant.ts     NOTIFICATION_REQUESTED = 'notification_requested'\n  notification-policy.constant.ts         defaults, digest window, quiet hours\n  notification-type.constant.ts           NOTIFICATION_TYPES (the enum-like list)\n  notification-watch-target-kind.constant.ts  RECORD | DOCUMENT | CHANNEL\ndtos/\n  notification.dto.ts                     GraphQL NotificationDTO\n  notification-watch.dto.ts               GraphQL NotificationWatchDTO\nlisteners/\n  notification-requested.listener.ts      @OnCustomBatchEvent(NOTIFICATION_REQUESTED)\n  notification-watch.listener.ts          @OnDatabaseBatchEvent(...) watch fan-out\n  __tests__/notification-requested.listener.spec.ts\n  __tests__/notification-watch.listener.spec.ts\nnotification.entity.ts                    core.notification table\nnotification-watch.entity.ts              core.notificationWatch table\nnotification.resolver.ts                  core /graphql inbox queries/mutations\nnotification-watch.resolver.ts            core /graphql watch queries/mutations\nnotification.module.ts                    Nest wiring\nnotification.resolver.spec.ts\nservices/\n  notification.service.ts                 producer seam + persistence + channels\n  notification-watch.service.ts           watch primitive + change→notification\n  notification-realtime-publisher.service.ts\n  notification-email-sender.service.ts\n  __tests__/*.spec.ts\ntypes/\n  notification-request.type.ts            NotificationRequest\n  notification-preferences.type.ts        NotificationPreferences\n  notification-dispatch-result.type.ts    NotificationDispatchResult\nutils/\n  build-watch-notification-payload.util.ts\n  group-notifications-into-digest-batches.util.ts\n  inbox-topic.util.ts\n  is-within-quiet-hours.util.ts\n  normalize-notification-preferences.util.ts\n  notification-email-item.util.ts\n  notification-realtime-event.util.ts\n  notification-to-dto.util.ts\n  resolve-notification-channel.util.ts\n  __tests__/*.spec.ts\n```\n\n### 1.2 The `NOTIFICATION_REQUESTED` event\n\n`constants/notification-event-name.constant.ts:4`\n```ts\nexport const NOTIFICATION_REQUESTED = 'notification_requested';\n```\n\nEmitted from `NotificationService.requestNotifications` (`services/notification.service.ts:47-59`):\n```ts\nrequestNotifications({ workspaceId, requests }: {\n  workspaceId: string;\n  requests: NotificationRequest[];\n}): void {\n  this.workspaceEventEmitter.emitCustomBatchEvent<NotificationRequest>(\n    NOTIFICATION_REQUESTED,\n    requests,\n    workspaceId,\n  );\n}\n```\n\nConsumed by `NotificationRequestedListener` (`listeners/notification-requested.listener.ts:23-56`):\n```ts\n@OnCustomBatchEvent(NOTIFICATION_REQUESTED)\nasync handleNotificationRequested(\n  payload: CustomWorkspaceEventBatch<NotificationRequest>,\n): Promise<void> {\n  if (!isDefined(payload.workspaceId)) return;\n  try {\n    const { inboxNotifications, emailDigestBatches } =\n      await this.notificationService.dispatchNotifications({\n        workspaceId: payload.workspaceId,\n        requests: payload.events,\n      });\n    await this.notificationRealtimePublisherService.publishInboxNotifications({\n      workspaceId: payload.workspaceId,\n      notifications: inboxNotifications,\n    });\n    await this.notificationEmailSenderService.sendEmailDigestBatches({\n      workspaceId: payload.workspaceId,\n      batches: emailDigestBatches,\n    });\n  } catch (error) {\n    // best-effort: never fail the producing domain flow\n    this.logger.error('Failed to dispatch notification requests', error);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 1.3 Notification entity — the row shape\n\n`notification.entity.ts:14-55` — the one durable inbox row. Note the comment at lines 14-16: `type` is a free string so a producer can ship a new type without a schema change.\n\n```ts\n@Entity({ name: 'notification', schema: 'core' })\n@ObjectType('Notification')\n@Index('IDX_NOTIFICATION_USER_ID_WORKSPACE_ID_CREATED_AT', ['userId','workspaceId','createdAt'])\n@Index('IDX_NOTIFICATION_USER_ID_WORKSPACE_ID_READ_AT', ['userId','workspaceId','readAt'])\nexport class NotificationEntity extends WorkspaceRelatedEntity {\n  @PrimaryGeneratedColumn('uuid') id: string;\n  @CreateDateColumn({ type: 'timestamptz' }) createdAt: Date;\n  @UpdateDateColumn({ type: 'timestamptz' }) updatedAt: Date;\n  @Column({ type: 'uuid', nullable: false }) userId: string;      // CORE USER, not workspace member\n  @Column({ type: 'varchar', nullable: false }) type: string;\n  @Column('jsonb', { nullable: true }) payload: Record<string, unknown> | null;\n  @Column({ type: 'timestamptz', nullable: true }) readAt: Date | null;\n  @Column({ type: 'timestamptz', nullable: true }) archivedAt: Date | null;\n}\n```\n\n`workspaceId` comes from `WorkspaceRelatedEntity` (`engine/workspace-manager/types/workspace-related-entity.ts:5-12`): `@Column({ nullable:false, type:'uuid' }) workspaceId: string;` plus a `WorkspaceEntity` relation.\n\n**Key point for US-156:** there is NO `recipientWorkspaceMemberId`, `label`, or `deepLink` column. The recipient is a core `userId`. Human-facing text and navigation are derived from `type` + the free-form `payload` JSON.\n\n### 1.4 How a notification is created (the exact insert shape)\n\n`NotificationRequest` (`types/notification-request.type.ts:3-10`):\n```ts\nexport type NotificationRequest = {\n  userId: string;\n  type: NotificationType;\n  payload: Record<string, unknown>;\n  createdAt?: Date;   // optional domain moment for digest windowing\n};\n```\n\n`NotificationService.dispatchNotifications` (`services/notification.service.ts:61-139`) is the persistence method. Per request it:\n1. resolves the user's channel via `resolveNotificationChannel` (line 90),\n2. `NONE` → `skippedByPreference++`,\n3. `EMAIL` → pushed to `emailCandidates`,\n4. otherwise `repository.create({...})` and later `save()`.\n\nThe literal insert values (`notification.service.ts:111-125`):\n```ts\ninboxRowsToCreate.push(\n  this.notificationRepository.create({\n    workspaceId,\n    userId: request.userId,\n    type: request.type,\n    payload: request.payload ?? null,\n    createdAt: request.createdAt ?? now,\n  }),\n);\n...\nconst inboxNotifications = inboxRowsToCreate.length > 0\n  ? await this.notificationRepository.save(inboxRowsToCreate)\n  : [];\n```\n\n`NotificationDispatchResult` (`types/notification-dispatch-result.type.ts:4-11`):\n```ts\nexport type NotificationDispatchResult = {\n  inboxNotifications: NotificationEntity[];\n  emailDigestBatches: NotificationEmailDigestBatch[];\n  suppressedByQuietHours: number;\n  skippedByPreference: number;\n};\n```\n\n### 1.5 Notification types / enums\n\n`constants/notification-type.constant.ts:3-18`:\n```ts\nexport const NOTIFICATION_TYPES = [\n  'MENTION',\n  'CHAT_MESSAGE',\n  'ASSIGNED',\n  'WATCHED_RECORD_CHANGED',\n  'BUDGET_ALERT',\n  'INVOICE_OVERDUE',\n  'PAYMENT_RECEIVED',\n  'SYSTEM',\n  'CALENDAR_REMINDER',\n] as const;\n\nexport type NotificationType = (typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES)[number];\n```\nThis is the authoritative `NotificationType` enum (a string-literal union, not a TS enum). `CALENDAR_REMINDER` was added last (P4C.4). US-156 would extend this list if it needs a new type; unknown types are stored but not preference-configurable.\n\nOther constants:\n- Channels (`notification-channel.constant.ts:1-3`): `['INBOX','EMAIL','NONE']`.\n- Watch target kinds (`notification-watch-target-kind.constant.ts:4-11`): `['RECORD','DOCUMENT','CHANNEL']`.\n- Policy (`notification-policy.constant.ts`): `DEFAULT_NOTIFICATION_CHANNEL='INBOX'` (line 3), `NOTIFICATION_EMAIL_DIGEST_WINDOW_MS = 15*60*1000` (line 10), default quiet hours 22:00→07:00 (lines 12-22).\n\n### 1.6 `NotificationWatchListener`\n\n`listeners/notification-watch.listener.ts` — hangs off the metadata engine's database events, one handler per watched object. Watched objects (lines 22-29): `document`, `note`, `task`, `opportunity`, `company`, `person`. Handlers:\n- `document` CREATED (line 47) and UPDATED (line 56) → `notifyCreated`/`notifyUpdated`\n- note/task/opportunity/company/person UPDATED (lines 63-96)\n- `chatMessage` CREATED (line 99) → channel watch, calls `notifyWatchersOfChange({ targetKind:'CHANNEL', targetId: channelId })`\n- helpers `notifyCreated` (122) / `notifyUpdated` (141) iterate `payload.events` and call `notificationWatchService.notifyWatchersOfChange({ workspaceId, targetKind, targetId, objectNameSingular, changedFieldNames })`\n- `resolveTargetKind` (line 174): `objectName === 'document' ? 'DOCUMENT' : 'RECORD'`.\n\n`NotificationWatchService.notifyWatchersOfChange` (`services/notification-watch.service.ts:144-216`) resolves watchers, ACL-prunes (`canUserReadTarget`, line 253; channels via `RealtimeTopicAccessService.canWorkspaceMemberReadChatChannel`, records/docs via `...canWorkspaceMemberReadObjectRecord`), then emits **one request per surviving watcher**:\n```ts\nthis.notificationService.requestNotifications({\n  workspaceId,\n  requests: permittedUserIds.map((userId) => ({\n    userId,\n    type: 'WATCHED_RECORD_CHANGED' as const,\n    payload: buildWatchNotificationPayload({ targetKind, objectNameSingular, targetId, changedFieldNames }),\n  })),\n});\n```\n\nWatch payload convention (`utils/build-watch-notification-payload.util.ts:10-39`):\n```ts\n{ kind: 'record.change', targetKind, changedFieldNames: [...] }\n// CHANNEL: { ...base, channelId: targetId }\n// RECORD/DOCUMENT: { ...base, objectNameSingular?, recordId: targetId }\n```\n\n## 2. Delivery / query over GraphQL, and the type values\n\n`NotificationResolver` (`notification.resolver.ts`) is a `@CoreResolver()` (must be `@CoreResolver` or it 404s at schema level, lines 19-22). All operations are caller-scoped (workspace+user from session):\n- Query `notifications(includeArchived): [NotificationDTO]` (line 30) → `NotificationService.findForUser`\n- Query `notificationUnreadCount: Int` (line 51) → `countUnread`\n- Mutation `markNotificationsAsRead(notificationIds: [UUID]): Int` (line 65)\n- Mutation `archiveNotifications(notificationIds: [UUID]): Int` (line 80)\n\n`NotificationDTO` (`dtos/notification.dto.ts:9-31`) exposes exactly: `id`, `type: string`, `payload: JSON|null` (`GraphQLJSON`), `createdAt`, `readAt`, `archivedAt`. The projection util is `notification-to-dto.util.ts` (drops `workspaceId`).\n\nRealtime delivery: `NotificationRealtimePublisherService.publishInboxNotifications` (`services/notification-realtime-publisher.service.ts:27-53`) groups notifications per user, recomputes unread via `countUnread`, publishes on topic `buildInboxTopic` = `workspace:<workspaceId>:inbox:<userId>` (`utils/inbox-topic.util.ts:6-12`) an event `NOTIFICATION_INBOX_UPDATED_EVENT_TYPE = 'notification.inbox.updated'` (`utils/notification-realtime-event.util.ts:8-9`) carrying `{ id, type, payload, createdAt, readAt, archivedAt }[]` + `unreadCount`.\n\nEmail delivery: `NotificationEmailSenderService` (`services/notification-email-sender.service.ts`) renders `twenty-emails` `NotificationEmail`/`NotificationDigestEmail`; labels come from `utils/notification-email-item.util.ts:11-24` (mirrors front-end labels), preview falls back through `PREVIEW_PAYLOAD_KEYS = ['preview','snippet','title']` (line 32).\n\nPreferences are stored per core user as a `KeyValuePairType.USER_VARIABLE` row under key `notification-preferences` (`notification.service.ts:23, 141-174`), normalized by `normalize-notification-preferences.util.ts`.\n\n### Front-end contract (important for payload design)\n`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/inbox/`:\n- `types/InboxNotification.ts`: `{ id, type: string, payload, createdAt, readAt, archivedAt }`; categories `all|mentions|assigned|watching`.\n- `utils/filterInboxNotificationsByCategory.ts:11-14`: `mentions:['MENTION']`, `assigned:['ASSIGNED']`, `watching:['WATCHED_RECORD_CHANGED']` — note **cross-app invoice/task notifications have no category today**.\n- `utils/resolveNotificationDeepLink.ts`: routes by payload `kind` (`chat.mention`/`chat.message` → Discussions with `channelId`), `CALENDAR_REMINDER` → `calendarEventId`, else `{ objectNameSingular, recordId }` → RecordShowPage; `null` = non-navigable.\n- `utils/getInboxNotificationPreview.ts`: `['preview','snippet','title']`.\n- Labels/icons switch in `components/InboxNotificationItem.tsx:119-165` (default fallback exists).\n\n## 3. Existing code that subscribes to workspace custom events and creates notifications\n\nProducers calling `NotificationService.requestNotifications` (search result):\n1. `src/modules/mention/services/mention-notification.service.ts:94-107` — type `'MENTION'`, payload via `buildMentionNotificationPayload`.\n2. `src/engine/core-modules/calendar/services/calendar-reminder.service.ts:175-188` — type `'CALENDAR_REMINDER'`, payload via `buildCalendarReminderNotificationPayload`.\n3. `src/engine/core-modules/notification/services/notification-watch.service.ts:201-213` — type `'WATCHED_RECORD_CHANGED'`.\n\nThe surface listeners that feed the mention engine (all `@OnDatabaseBatchEvent`):\n- `src/modules/chat/listeners/chat-mention.listener.ts:21` (`chatMessage` CREATED) → `ChatMentionService`.\n- `src/modules/mention/listeners/document-mention.listener.ts:35,49` (`document` CREATED/UPDATED, only when `content` changed).\n- `src/modules/mention/listeners/document-comment-mention.listener.ts:35,49` (`documentCommentThread` CREATED/UPDATED, only when `comments` changed).\n\n`MentionNotificationService` (`src/modules/mention/services/mention-notification.service.ts`) parses by surface, resolves workspaceMember→userId (`resolveMentionTargets`, lines 115-144), permission-filters via `MentionAccessService`, then emits per permitted user (lines 94-107):\n```ts\nthis.notificationService.requestNotifications({\n  workspaceId,\n  requests: permittedTargets.map((target) => ({\n    userId: target.userId,\n    type: 'MENTION' as const,\n    payload: buildMentionNotificationPayload({ source, authorId, mentionedWorkspaceMemberIds, contextSnippet }),\n    ...(createdAt === undefined ? {} : { createdAt }),\n  })),\n});\n```\n\nMention payload shapes (`src/modules/mention/utils/build-mention-notification-payload.util.ts:17-49`):\n```ts\nbase = { kind: `${surface}.mention`, authorId, mentionedWorkspaceMemberIds, snippet }\nchat:    { ...base, channelId, messageId }\ndocument:{ ...base, objectNameSingular:'document', recordId: documentId, documentId }\ncomment: { ...base, objectNameSingular:'document', recordId: documentId, documentId, threadId }\n```\n`MentionSource` union: `src/modules/mention/types/mention.type.ts:10-13`.\n\nThe only raw `@OnEvent(...)` users (not the batch wrappers) are `engine/subscriptions/metadata-event/metadata-events-to-db.listener.ts:26,33,40` and `engine/subscriptions/queue-job-event/queue-job-event.listener.ts:24`.\n\nThe mention module wiring: `src/modules/mention/mention.module.ts` imports `NotificationModule`, `RealtimeGatewayModule`, `UserWorkspaceModule`; exports `MentionNotificationService`. `NotificationModule` exports `NotificationService` and `NotificationWatchService` (`notification.module.ts:38`).\n\n## 4. `WorkspaceEventEmitter`, `OnDatabaseBatchEvent`, and cross-app events (US-155)\n\n### 4.1 `WorkspaceEventEmitter`\n\n`src/engine/workspace-event-emitter/workspace-event-emitter.ts` (module is `@Global`, `workspace-event-emitter.module.ts:5-10`):\n```ts\n@Injectable()\nexport class WorkspaceEventEmitter {\n  constructor(private readonly eventEmitter: EventEmitter2) {}\n\n  public emitDatabaseBatchEvent<T, A extends keyof ActionEventMap<T>>(\n    databaseBatchEventInput: DatabaseBatchEventInput<T, A> | undefined,\n  ) { ... }  // computes `${object}.${action}` and emits WorkspaceEventBatch (lines 42-71)\n\n  public emitCustomBatchEvent<T extends object>(\n    eventName: CustomEventName,\n    events: T[],\n    workspaceId: string | undefined,\n  ) {\n    if (!events.length) return;\n    const customWorkspaceEventBatch: CustomWorkspaceEventBatch<T> = {\n      name: eventName, workspaceId, events,\n    };\n    this.eventEmitter.emit(eventName, customWorkspaceEventBatch);   // lines 73-89\n  }\n}\n```\n\nTypes:\n- `CustomEventName = \\`${string}_${string}\\`` (`types/custom-event-name.type.ts:1`) — hence event names use underscores.\n- `CustomWorkspaceEventBatch<T> = { name: string; workspaceId?: string; events: T[] }` (`types/custom-workspace-batch-event.type.ts:1-5`).\n- `WorkspaceEventBatch<T> = { name; workspaceId: string; objectMetadata: FlatObjectMetadata; events: T[] }` (`types/workspace-event-batch.type.ts:3-8`).\n- `computeEventName` (`utils/compute-event-name.ts:3-9`) → `${objectName}.${action}` guarded by `checkStringIsDatabaseEventAction`.\n\n### 4.2 Decorators\n\n- `OnDatabaseBatchEvent(object, action)` (`engine/api/graphql/graphql-query-runner/decorators/on-database-batch-event.decorator.ts:5-18`) → `OnEvent(`${object}.${action}`)`. `object` may be `'*'` (wildcard; used by cross-app listener and workflow triggers).\n- `OnCustomBatchEvent(event)` (`.../on-custom-batch-event.decorator.ts:5-13`) → `OnEvent(event)`.\n- `DatabaseEventAction` enum (`.../enums/database-event-action.ts:3-10`): `created | updated | deleted | destroyed | restored | upserted`.\n\n### 4.3 Cross-app events module (server)\n\nRoot: `packages/twenty-server/src/modules/cross-app-events/`\n```\nconstants/cross-app-lifecycle-event.constant.ts\ncross-app-events.module.ts\nlisteners/cross-app-lifecycle-event.listener.ts\nlisteners/__tests__/cross-app-lifecycle-event.listener.spec.ts\nservices/cross-app-event-emitter.service.ts\nservices/__tests__/cross-app-event-emitter.service.spec.ts\nutils/map-database-event-to-cross-app-events.util.ts\nutils/__tests__/map-database-event-to-cross-app-events.util.spec.ts\n__tests__/cross-app-lifecycle-contract.spec.ts\n```\n\n`CROSS_APP_LIFECYCLE_EVENT` — `constants/cross-app-lifecycle-event.constant.ts:4`:\n```ts\nexport const CROSS_APP_LIFECYCLE_EVENT = 'cross_app_lifecycle';\n```\n(underscore style, matches `CustomEventName`).\n\n**There is currently no subscriber to this event.** Grep for `CROSS_APP_LIFECYCLE_EVENT` returns only the constant, the emitter service, and tests. US-156 is described (phase-15 report line 138/140) as the task that \"subscribes `@OnEvent(CROSS_APP_LIFECYCLE_EVENT)`\".\n\n`CrossAppLifecycleEventListener` (`listeners/cross-app-lifecycle-event.listener.ts`) subscribes to **every** database event via wildcard, one handler per action:\n```ts\n@OnDatabaseBatchEvent('*', DatabaseEventAction.CREATED)   // line 22\n@OnDatabaseBatchEvent('*', DatabaseEventAction.UPDATED)   // line 29\n@OnDatabaseBatchEvent('*', DatabaseEventAction.DELETED)   // line 36\n@OnDatabaseBatchEvent('*', DatabaseEventAction.DESTROYED) // line 43\n@OnDatabaseBatchEvent('*', DatabaseEventAction.RESTORED)  // line 50\n@OnDatabaseBatchEvent('*', DatabaseEventAction.UPSERTED)  // line 57\n```\nEach calls `emitSafely` (line 66) → `CrossAppEventEmitterService.emitCrossAppEvents({ workspaceId, objectMetadataNameSingular: payload.objectMetadata.nameSingular, databaseAction, events: payload.events })`, logging/swallowing errors (best-effort).\n\n`CrossAppEventEmitterService` (`services/cross-app-event-emitter.service.ts`):\n- Input type `EmitCrossAppEventsInput` (lines 13-18): `{ workspaceId, objectMetadataNameSingular, databaseAction, events: ObjectRecordEvent[] }`.\n- Rejects objects outside the contract via `resolveCrossAppEventObjectFamily` before touching cache (lines 39-43).\n- Reads installed apps from `WorkspaceCacheService.getOrRecompute(workspaceId, ['flatApplicationMaps'])` and builds `Set(idByUniversalIdentifier keys)` (lines 45-54).\n- Maps via `mapDatabaseEventToCrossAppEvents` (line 56).\n- Emits `workspaceEventEmitter.emitCustomBatchEvent(CROSS_APP_LIFECYCLE_EVENT, crossAppEvents, workspaceId)` (lines 70-74).\n\n`mapDatabaseEventToCrossAppEvents` (`utils/map-database-event-to-cross-app-events.util.ts`):\n- `DATABASE_ACTION_TO_CROSS_APP_ACTION` map (lines 22-32): created→created; updated/restored/upserted→updated; deleted/destroyed→deleted.\n- `CROSS_APP_EVENT_COMPLETED_TASK_STATUS = 'DONE'` (line 20). `resolveAction` (lines 77-109) promotes a task UPDATED whose `status` goes non-DONE → `DONE` to the semantic action `'completed'`.\n- `resolveActor` (lines 63-72): `{ type:'workspaceMember', workspaceMemberId, userWorkspaceId? }` when `event.workspaceMemberId` is non-empty, else `{ type:'system' }`.\n- Reads snapshot from `properties.after ?? properties.before` (lines 43-55), `createdAt`/`updatedAt` timestamps (lines 57-61).\n- Install gating (lines 125-133): if `CROSS_APP_EVENT_ACTIVATION_APP_BY_FAMILY[objectFamily]` is defined and the app is not installed → emits nothing.\n- Skips events without a non-empty `recordId` (lines 138-140).\n\n### 4.4 Shared cross-app contract (`packages/twenty-shared/src/cross-app-events/`)\n\nFiles:\n```\nbuild-cross-app-event-payload.util.ts\ncompute-cross-app-event-name.util.ts\ncross-app-event-action.type.ts\ncross-app-event-actor.type.ts\ncross-app-event-name.type.ts\ncross-app-event-object-family.type.ts\ncross-app-event-payload.type.ts\ncross-app-event-timestamps.type.ts\ncross-app-event-vocabulary.constant.ts\nindex.ts\nis-cross-app-event-action.util.ts\nis-cross-app-event-object-family.util.ts\nis-cross-app-event-payload.util.ts\nresolve-cross-app-event-object-family.util.ts\n__tests__/cross-app-events-contract.spec.ts\n```\n\n**Exact event name format** — `compute-cross-app-event-name.util.ts:5-8`:\n```ts\nexport const computeCrossAppEventName = (\n  objectFamily: CrossAppEventObjectFamily,\n  action: CrossAppEventAction,\n): CrossAppEventName => `${objectFamily}.${action}`;\n```\nType `CrossAppEventName = \\`${CrossAppEventObjectFamily}.${CrossAppEventAction}\\`` (`cross-app-event-name.type.ts:7-8`). So `CrossAppEventPayload.name` is e.g. `document.created`, `task.completed`, `calendarEvent.updated`, `file.created`, `invoice.created`.\n\n**Family → object-name map** — `cross-app-event-vocabulary.constant.ts:20-29`:\n```ts\nexport const CROSS_APP_EVENT_OBJECT_NAME_BY_FAMILY: Record<CrossAppEventObjectFamily, string> = {\n  document: 'document',\n  task: 'task',\n  calendarEvent: 'calendarEvent',\n  file: 'attachment',   // file rides the standard attachment object\n  invoice: 'invoice',\n};\n```\n\n**Activation-app map** — `cross-app-event-vocabulary.constant.ts:35-40`:\n```ts\nexport const CROSS_APP_EVENT_ACTIVATION_APP_BY_FAMILY: Partial<Record<CrossAppEventObjectFamily, string>> = {\n  document: '19126a9c-7cc0-4368-aaba-c7e5a87b0c48',   // a2e-documents\n  invoice:  'b11a0000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001',   // a2e-accounting\n};\n```\n`task`, `calendarEvent`, `file` are ungated (standard objects). Also `CROSS_APP_EVENT_CONTRACT_VERSION = 1` (line 6), `CROSS_APP_EVENT_OBJECT_FAMILIES = ['document','task','calendarEvent','file','invoice']` (lines 8-9), `CROSS_APP_EVENT_ACTIONS = ['created','updated','completed','deleted']` (lines 11-16).\n\n**Types**:\n- `CrossAppEventObjectFamily` (`cross-app-event-object-family.type.ts:5-10`): `'document'|'task'|'calendarEvent'|'file'|'invoice'`.\n- `CrossAppEventAction` (`cross-app-event-action.type.ts:4-8`): `'created'|'updated'|'completed'|'deleted'`.\n- `CrossAppEventActor` (`cross-app-event-actor.type.ts:4-8`): `{ type:'workspaceMember'|'system'; workspaceMemberId?: string; userWorkspaceId?: string }`.\n- `CrossAppEventTimestamps` (`cross-app-event-timestamps.type.ts:4-8`): `{ occurredAt: string; createdAt: string|null; updatedAt: string|null }`.\n- `CrossAppEventPayload<TRecord = Record<string, unknown>>` (`cross-app-event-payload.type.ts:11-21`):\n```ts\nexport type CrossAppEventPayload<TRecord = Record<string, unknown>> = {\n  contractVersion: number;\n  name: CrossAppEventName;\n  workspaceId: string;\n  objectFamily: CrossAppEventObjectFamily;\n  action: CrossAppEventAction;\n  recordId: string;\n  actor: CrossAppEventActor;\n  timestamps: CrossAppEventTimestamps;\n  record: TRecord;   // before/after snapshot\n};\n```\n\n**Payload builder** — `build-cross-app-event-payload.util.ts`:\n```ts\nexport type BuildCrossAppEventPayloadInput<TRecord = Record<string, unknown>> = {\n  objectFamily; action; workspaceId; recordId; actor; timestamps; record;\n};\n\nexport const buildCrossAppEventPayload = <TRecord = Record<string, unknown>>(\n  input: BuildCrossAppEventPayloadInput<TRecord>,\n): CrossAppEventPayload<TRecord> => ({\n  contractVersion: CROSS_APP_EVENT_CONTRACT_VERSION,\n  name: computeCrossAppEventName(input.objectFamily, input.action),\n  workspaceId: input.workspaceId,\n  objectFamily: input.objectFamily,\n  action: input.action,\n  recordId: input.recordId,\n  actor: input.actor,\n  timestamps: input.timestamps,\n  record: input.record,\n});\n```\n\nRuntime guard `isCrossAppEventPayload` (`is-cross-app-event-payload.util.ts:9-31`) validates `contractVersion`, `name === \\`${objectFamily}.${action}\\``, actor/timestamps object shape — this is what a US-156 subscriber can use to reject malformed bus payloads.\n\n`resolveCrossAppEventObjectFamily` (`resolve-cross-app-event-object-family.util.ts:7-17`) reverse-maps a singular object name → family; `isCrossAppEventAction`/`isCrossAppEventObjectFamily` are the narrowing guards.\n\n### 4.5 Wiring\n\n- `WorkspaceEventEmitterModule` is `@Global` (`workspace-event-emitter.module.ts`).\n- `CrossAppEventsModule` (`cross-app-events.module.ts`): imports `WorkspaceCacheModule`; providers `CrossAppEventEmitterService`, `CrossAppLifecycleEventListener`; exports only `CrossAppEventEmitterService` (not the listener/constant).\n- Registered in `src/modules/modules.module.ts:5,16`.\n- `MentionModule`/`ChatModule` import `NotificationModule`; `NotificationModule` imports `KeyValuePairModule`, `RealtimeGatewayModule`, `EmailModule`, `WorkspaceDomainsModule`, `UserWorkspaceModule`, `WorkspaceCacheModule`, and `TypeOrmModule.forFeature([NotificationEntity, NotificationWatchEntity, UserEntity, WorkspaceEntity])`. `NotificationModule` and `MentionModule` are both in `core-engine.module.ts:151-152`.\n\n## Key implications / gaps for US-156\n\n- **One seam to target:** call `NotificationService.requestNotifications({ workspaceId, requests: NotificationRequest[] })` (or add a subscriber that receives `CROSS_APP_LIFECYCLE_EVENT` and does so). The `NotificationRequest` is `{ userId, type, payload, createdAt? }` — there is no memberId/label/deepLink field.\n- **No existing cross-app subscriber:** `CROSS_APP_LIFECYCLE_EVENT` is emitted but nobody listens. US-156 must add one (likely `@OnCustomBatchEvent(CROSS_APP_LIFECYCLE_EVENT)` in a new listener, since the batch wrapper carries `workspaceId`; `@OnEvent` works too but the typed wrapper is preferred).\n- **`CustomWorkspaceEventBatch<CrossAppEventPayload>`** carries `workspaceId` and `events[]`; each event already contains `workspaceId`, `recordId`, `objectFamily`, `action`, `actor.workspaceMemberId`, `timestamps`, and `record`. Mapping to recipients requires workspaceMember→userId resolution (there is no built-in util; `MentionNotificationService.resolveMentionTargets` and `CalendarReminderService.resolveOwnerUserIds` both do this via `workspaceOrmManager`/`WorkspaceCacheService.flatWorkspaceMemberMaps`).\n- **NotificationType coverage:** existing types cover mentions/chat/assigned/watch/finance/calendar/system. Bilan approvals would need either a new type in `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` (plus front-end label/icon/category and email label) or reuse of `INVOICE_OVERDUE`/`SYSTEM`. Unknown types still store but are not preference-configurable and have no front-end category.\n- **Payload convention to follow:** front-end deep-linking reads `payload.kind`, `channelId`, `messageId`, or `{ objectNameSingular, recordId }`, plus `calendarEventId` for reminders; previews read `preview|snippet|title`. For cross-app records, use `{ kind, objectNameSingular, recordId, ... }` (object name must be a native page, e.g. `task`, `invoice`, `document`); note `file` maps to object `attachment`.\n- **Idempotency / best-effort pattern:** producers wrap their fan-out in try/catch and log (never fail the domain write); the listener `NotificationRequestedListener` also swallows errors. Mention edits de-dupe via `excludeWorkspaceMemberIds`; calendar reminders claim `reminderDeliveredAt` before notifying. Cross-app events already emit on every lifecycle action, so US-156 must decide its own de-dup/`updatedFields` gating.\n</task_result>\n</task>",
