      "errorMessage": "<task id=\"ses_f06839045ffeYFmHS4YKPPaWsO\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nI have completed a thorough exploration. Here is the full report.\n\n---\n\n# Native Inbox / Notifications on the Front (`twenty-front`)\n\n## 0. TL;DR for US-156\n\n- The front inbox is a **core-schema, hand-written GraphQL** feature. There is **no generated GraphQL type or hook for notifications** and **no front-end notification-type enum** — `InboxNotification.type` is a raw `string`, and every mapping is inline `switch`/string-literal.\n- The canonical type taxonomy lives **server-side** at `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/notification/constants/notification-type.constant.ts` (`NOTIFICATION_TYPES` + `NotificationType`). `ObjectRecordUpdate` does **not** exist anywhere in this repo (that is upstream Twenty naming; this codebase uses `WATCHED_RECORD_CHANGED`).\n- Deep links are resolved by **payload shape**, not by type (except `CALENDAR_REMINDER`): `{objectNameSingular, recordId}`, chat `{channelId, messageId}`, or `{calendarEventId}`.\n- Currently only 3 types have producers: `MENTION`, `CALENDAR_REMINDER`, `WATCHED_RECORD_CHANGED`. `ASSIGNED`, `SYSTEM`, `CHAT_MESSAGE`, `INVOICE_OVERDUE`, `PAYMENT_RECEIVED`, `BUDGET_ALERT` exist only as labels/constants/tests — **no producer**. No Bilan/approval producer exists at all.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Inventory: `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/inbox/**`\n\n| Path | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `components/InboxNotificationItem.tsx` | Row: label, icon, preview, unread dot, calendar extras, click→open |\n| `components/InboxNotificationList.tsx` | Day-grouped list + empty state |\n| `components/InboxFilterTabs.tsx` | All / Mentions / Assigned / Watching tabs |\n| `components/InboxBulkActions.tsx` | Mark-as-read / Archive / Clear bar |\n| `components/__tests__/InboxNotificationItem.test.tsx` | Row tests (calendar reminder focus) |\n| `graphql/queries/inboxNotificationsQuery.ts` | `notifications(includeArchived)` query + result type |\n| `graphql/queries/inboxUnreadCountQuery.ts` | `notificationUnreadCount` query |\n| `graphql/mutations/archiveInboxNotificationsMutation.ts` | `archiveNotifications` mutation |\n| `graphql/mutations/markInboxNotificationsAsReadMutation.ts` | `markNotificationsAsRead` mutation |\n| `hooks/useInboxNotifications.ts` | Loads list via Apollo |\n| `hooks/useInboxUnreadCount.ts` | Loads unread count |\n| `hooks/useInboxLive.ts` | Subscribes to realtime topic |\n| `hooks/useInboxBulkActions.ts` | Bulk mutations + refetch |\n| `types/InboxNotification.ts` | `InboxNotification`, `InboxNotificationPayload`, `InboxNotificationCategory` |\n| `types/InboxRealtimeEvent.ts` | Realtime event contract |\n| `utils/resolveNotificationDeepLink.ts` | **Deep-link resolver** |\n| `utils/filterInboxNotificationsByCategory.ts` | Category→type mapping |\n| `utils/getInboxNotificationPreview.ts` | Preview extraction |\n| `utils/groupInboxNotificationsByDay.ts` | Day grouping / sort |\n| `utils/parseCalendarReminderNotificationPayload.ts` | Calendar payload parser |\n| `utils/formatCalendarReminderStart.ts` | ISO→local string |\n| `utils/applyInboxRealtimeEventToNotifications.ts` | Idempotent realtime fold |\n| `utils/buildInboxTopic.ts` | Topic string builder |\n| `utils/__tests__/*` | 6 test files (deep-link, filter, group, parse, format, realtime, topic) |\n\nThe page that composes it all is outside the module: `packages/twenty-front/src/pages/inbox/InboxPage.tsx`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. `resolveNotificationDeepLink.ts` — exact code\n\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/inbox/utils/resolveNotificationDeepLink.ts` (73 lines):\n\n```ts\nimport { AppPath, CoreObjectNameSingular } from 'twenty-shared/types';\nimport { getAppPath, isDefined } from 'twenty-shared/utils';\n\nimport { type InboxNotification } from '@/inbox/types/InboxNotification';\n\nconst getPayloadString = (\n  payload: Record<string, unknown>,\n  key: string,\n): string | null => {\n  const value = payload[key];\n\n  return typeof value === 'string' && value.length > 0 ? value : null;\n};\n\n// Maps a notification to the native route of its target. Only producers that\n// exist resolve: chat mentions/messages land on the discussions page (P5.2),\n// and record/document notifications follow the `{ objectNameSingular, recordId }`\n// payload convention (records/documents are native). Anything else — an unknown\n// type or a payload missing its ids — returns null so the inbox renders a\n// non-navigable, graceful state instead of a broken link.\nexport const resolveNotificationDeepLink = (\n  notification: InboxNotification,\n): string | null => {\n  const payload = notification.payload;\n\n  if (payload === null) {\n    return null;\n  }\n\n  // A calendar reminder names its event by `calendarEventId` (not the record\n  // `{ objectNameSingular, recordId }` convention), and the event is a native\n  // record, so it opens on the calendarEvent record page.\n  if (notification.type === 'CALENDAR_REMINDER') {\n    const calendarEventId = getPayloadString(payload, 'calendarEventId');\n\n    return isDefined(calendarEventId)\n      ? getAppPath(AppPath.RecordShowPage, {\n          objectNameSingular: CoreObjectNameSingular.CalendarEvent,\n          objectRecordId: calendarEventId,\n        })\n      : null;\n  }\n\n  const kind = getPayloadString(payload, 'kind');\n  const channelId = getPayloadString(payload, 'channelId');\n\n  if (kind === 'chat.mention' || kind === 'chat.message') {\n    return isDefined(channelId)\n      ? getAppPath(AppPath.Discussions, undefined, { channelId })\n      : null;\n  }\n\n  // Defensive fallback: a chat payload without a `kind` still deep-links as\n  // long as it carries a channel and a message.\n  if (\n    isDefined(channelId) &&\n    isDefined(getPayloadString(payload, 'messageId'))\n  ) {\n    return getAppPath(AppPath.Discussions, undefined, { channelId });\n  }\n\n  const objectNameSingular = getPayloadString(payload, 'objectNameSingular');\n  const recordId = getPayloadString(payload, 'recordId');\n\n  if (isDefined(objectNameSingular) && isDefined(recordId)) {\n    return getAppPath(AppPath.RecordShowPage, {\n      objectNameSingular,\n      objectRecordId: recordId,\n    });\n  }\n\n  return null;\n};\n```\n\n### Deep-link resolution order (by priority)\n\n| Order | Condition | Resulting path |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | `payload === null` | `null` |\n| 1 | `type === 'CALENDAR_REMINDER'` and `payload.calendarEventId` | `/object/calendarEvent/<id>` (uses `CoreObjectNameSingular.CalendarEvent`) |\n| 2 | `payload.kind === 'chat.mention' \\| 'chat.message'` and `payload.channelId` | `/discussions?channelId=<id>` |\n| 3 | any payload with `channelId` + `messageId` (defensive) | `/discussions?channelId=<id>` |\n| 4 | `payload.objectNameSingular` + `payload.recordId` | `/object/<objectNameSingular>/<recordId>` |\n| 5 | otherwise | `null` (row renders non-actionable) |\n\nPath constants come from `twenty-shared`:\n- `AppPath.Discussions = '/discussions'` — `packages/twenty-shared/src/types/AppPath.ts:24`\n- `AppPath.RecordShowPage = '/object/:objectNameSingular/:objectRecordId'` — `AppPath.ts:40`\n- `AppPath.Inbox = '/inbox'` — `AppPath.ts:26`\n- `CoreObjectNameSingular.CalendarEvent = 'calendarEvent'` — `packages/twenty-shared/src/types/CoreObjectNameSingular.ts:8`\n- `getAppPath` builds params + query string via `react-router-dom` `generatePath` and `qs` — `packages/twenty-shared/src/utils/navigation/getAppPath.ts:6-30`\n\nNote: there is **no type-based route for `MENTION`** — mentions resolve purely on payload (`kind`/`channelId` or `objectNameSingular`/`recordId`). `AppPath.Bureau` (`/bureau`, AppPath.ts:28) is **not** used by any resolver.\n\nThe test file (`utils/__tests__/resolveNotificationDeepLink.test.ts`) asserts these exact strings: `/discussions?channelId=channel-1` (L26), `/object/task/task-1` (L45), `/object/document/document-1` (L56), `/object/calendarEvent/event-1` (L67), and null cases (L75, L81, L86, L93, L101).\n\n---\n\n## 3. `InboxNotificationItem.tsx` — exact type→label/icon code\n\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/inbox/components/InboxNotificationItem.tsx` (235 lines). Icons imported at lines 4-13 (`IconAlertTriangle, IconArchive, IconAt, IconBell, IconCalendarEvent, IconCheckbox, IconEye, IconMessage` from `twenty-ui/icon`).\n\nDeep link / actionability (L116-117):\n\n```tsx\nconst deepLink = resolveNotificationDeepLink(notification);\nconst isActionable = deepLink !== null;\n```\n\n### Label switch (L119-142)\n\n```tsx\nconst getNotificationLabel = () => {\n  switch (notification.type) {\n    case 'MENTION':                return t`You were mentioned`;\n    case 'CHAT_MESSAGE':           return t`New message`;\n    case 'ASSIGNED':               return t`Assigned to you`;\n    case 'WATCHED_RECORD_CHANGED': return t`A watched record changed`;\n    case 'CALENDAR_REMINDER':      return t`Calendar event reminder`;\n    case 'INVOICE_OVERDUE':        return t`An invoice is overdue`;\n    case 'PAYMENT_RECEIVED':       return t`A payment was received`;\n    case 'BUDGET_ALERT':           return t`A budget threshold was reached`;\n    case 'SYSTEM':                 return t`System notification`;\n    default:                       return t`Notification`;\n  }\n};\n```\n\n### Icon switch (L144-165)\n\n```tsx\nconst getNotificationIcon = () => {\n  switch (notification.type) {\n    case 'MENTION':                return <IconAt size={16} />;\n    case 'CHAT_MESSAGE':           return <IconMessage size={16} />;\n    case 'ASSIGNED':               return <IconCheckbox size={16} />;\n    case 'WATCHED_RECORD_CHANGED': return <IconEye size={16} />;\n    case 'CALENDAR_REMINDER':      return <IconCalendarEvent size={16} />;\n    case 'INVOICE_OVERDUE':\n    case 'PAYMENT_RECEIVED':\n    case 'BUDGET_ALERT':           return <IconAlertTriangle size={16} />;\n    case 'SYSTEM':                 return <IconArchive size={16} />;\n    default:                       return <IconBell size={16} />;\n  }\n};\n```\n\n### Full type→label/icon/deep-link matrix\n\n| Type | Label (`t`) | Icon | Deep link? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `MENTION` | `You were mentioned` | `IconAt` | Payload-driven (chat→`/discussions?channelId=`, doc→`/object/document/`) |\n| `CHAT_MESSAGE` | `New message` | `IconMessage` | Payload-driven (chat keys) |\n| `ASSIGNED` | `Assigned to you` | `IconCheckbox` | Payload-driven (`objectNameSingular`+`recordId`) |\n| `WATCHED_RECORD_CHANGED` | `A watched record changed` | `IconEye` | Payload-driven |\n| `CALENDAR_REMINDER` | `Calendar event reminder` | `IconCalendarEvent` | `calendarEventId` → `/object/calendarEvent/<id>` |\n| `INVOICE_OVERDUE` | `An invoice is overdue` | `IconAlertTriangle` | Payload-driven (no producer yet) |\n| `PAYMENT_RECEIVED` | `A payment was received` | `IconAlertTriangle` | Payload-driven (no producer yet) |\n| `BUDGET_ALERT` | `A budget threshold was reached` | `IconAlertTriangle` | Payload-driven (no producer yet) |\n| `SYSTEM` | `System notification` | `IconArchive` | Payload-driven (no producer yet) |\n| *(unknown)* | `Notification` | `IconBell` | Payload-driven |\n\n### Preview + calendar extras (L167-183)\n\n```tsx\nconst preview = getInboxNotificationPreview(notification);\n\nconst calendarReminder =\n  notification.type === 'CALENDAR_REMINDER'\n    ? parseCalendarReminderNotificationPayload(notification.payload)\n    : null;\n\nconst calendarReminderStartLabel = isDefined(calendarReminder)\n  ? formatCalendarReminderStart(calendarReminder.startsAt)\n  : null;\n\nconst calendarReminderLeadLabel =\n  isDefined(calendarReminder) && calendarReminder.reminderMinutes !== null\n    ? calendarReminder.reminderMinutes === 0\n      ? t`At the time of the event`\n      : t`${calendarReminder.reminderMinutes} min before`\n    : null;\n```\n\n### Render behavior (L185-234)\n\n- Root `StyledRow` with `data-testid={`inbox-notification-${notification.id}`}` (L188).\n- `Checkbox` for selection, `aria-label={t`Select notification`}` (L190-194).\n- `StyledContent` is a `<button type=\"button\" disabled={!isActionable}>`; onClick calls `onOpenNotification(notification)` only when actionable (L195-203).\n- Title shows label + unread dot if `notification.readAt === null` (L206-209).\n- If actionable → preview rendered; if **not** actionable → `t`This notification has no destination`` (L210-216).\n- Calendar `Starts <label>` and lead label rendered only when actionable (L217-224).\n- Time rendered via `new Date(createdAt).toLocaleTimeString([], {hour:'2-digit', minute:'2-digit'})` (L226-231).\n\nThe test (`components/__tests__/InboxNotificationItem.test.tsx`) asserts label `Calendar event reminder` (L56), `.tabler-icon-calendar-event` (L57-59), `15 min before` / `At the time of the event` (L67,73), `This notification has no destination` (L95,108), and non-actionable click does not open (L86-101).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Types\n\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/inbox/types/InboxNotification.ts` (18 lines, full):\n\n```ts\nexport type InboxNotificationPayload = Record<string, unknown> | null;\n\nexport type InboxNotification = {\n  id: string;\n  type: string;                 // <-- raw string, NOT an enum/union on the front\n  payload: InboxNotificationPayload;\n  createdAt: string;\n  readAt: string | null;\n  archivedAt: string | null;\n};\n\n// The four inbox filter tabs. A category maps to one or more persisted\n// notification types in `filterInboxNotificationsByCategory`.\nexport type InboxNotificationCategory =\n  | 'all'\n  | 'mentions'\n  | 'assigned'\n  | 'watching';\n```\n\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/inbox/types/InboxRealtimeEvent.ts` (16 lines, full):\n\n```ts\nimport { type InboxNotification } from '@/inbox/types/InboxNotification';\n\nexport const INBOX_UPDATED_EVENT_TYPE = 'notification.inbox.updated';\n\nexport type InboxRealtimeEvent = {\n  type: typeof INBOX_UPDATED_EVENT_TYPE;\n  workspaceId: string;\n  userId: string;\n  occurredAt: string;\n  unreadCount: number;\n  notifications: InboxNotification[];\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Category filtering\n\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/inbox/utils/filterInboxNotificationsByCategory.ts:7-19`:\n\n```ts\nconst INBOX_CATEGORY_TYPES: Record<\n  Exclude<InboxNotificationCategory, 'all'>,\n  string[]\n> = {\n  mentions: ['MENTION'],\n  assigned: ['ASSIGNED'],\n  watching: ['WATCHED_RECORD_CHANGED'],\n};\n\nexport const getInboxCategoryTypes = (category) =>\n  category === 'all' ? null : INBOX_CATEGORY_TYPES[category];\n```\n\nThis is the only place front types are enumerated (as raw string literals). New US-156 types (e.g. approval, task mention) land in `all` only unless added to a category.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Hooks\n\n- `useInboxNotifications.ts:12-29` — `useQuery<InboxNotificationsQueryResult>(INBOX_NOTIFICATIONS_QUERY, { client: apolloCoreClient, variables: { includeArchived } })`; returns `notifications: data?.notifications ?? []`, `loading`, `error`.\n- `useInboxUnreadCount.ts:12-25` — query `INBOX_UNREAD_COUNT_QUERY`, returns `unreadCount: data?.notificationUnreadCount ?? 0`.\n- `useInboxLive.ts:15-36` — builds topic `workspace:<id>:inbox:<userId>` from `currentWorkspaceState` + `currentUserState` and calls `useRealtimeTopic<InboxRealtimeEvent>({ topic, enabled, onEvent })`. **Uses core `currentUser.id`, not workspace member id** (comment L12-14).\n- `useInboxBulkActions.ts:12-56` — `markAsRead`/`archive` mutations, each refetching `INBOX_NOTIFICATIONS_QUERY` + `INBOX_UNREAD_COUNT_QUERY` with `awaitRefetchQueries: true`.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Page wiring: `InboxPage.tsx`\n\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/pages/inbox/InboxPage.tsx` (218 lines):\n\n- State: `selectedCategory` (L69), `selectedNotificationIds` (L71), `realtimeEvents` (L74).\n- Data: `useInboxNotifications()` (L78), `useInboxUnreadCount()` (L83), `useInboxBulkActions()` (L84).\n- `useInboxLive` appends events (L86-89); `notifications` = reduce realtime events over loaded rows (L93-104).\n- `unreadCount` prefers last realtime event's count (L106-111).\n- `countByCategory` per tab (L113-130); `filteredNotifications` (L132-139); `dayGroups` (L141-144).\n- **`handleOpenNotification` (L159-171)** — the click handler:\n\n```tsx\nconst handleOpenNotification = (notification: InboxNotification) => {\n  const deepLink = resolveNotificationDeepLink(notification);\n  if (deepLink === null) { return; }\n  if (notification.readAt === null) { void markAsRead([notification.id]); }\n  navigate(deepLink);\n};\n```\n\n- Route registration: `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/app/routing/utils/createWorkspaceRouteObjects.tsx:168-175` maps `AppPath.Inbox` → lazy `InboxPage`.\n- `AppPath.Inbox` listed in `packages/twenty-front/src/testing/constants/UntestedAppPaths.ts:15`.\n- Chat deep link target reads the query param: `packages/twenty-front/src/pages/chat/ChatPage.tsx:63` `const requestedChannelId = searchParams.get('channelId');` (comment L61-62 confirms this is the \"Go to channel\" link). `isDiscussionsPath` at `packages/twenty-front/src/utils/isDiscussionsPath.ts`.\n\n---\n\n## 8. GraphQL — hand-written, no generated types/hooks\n\nAll four operations are hand-written (comment at `inboxNotificationsQuery.ts:5-7`: \"the notification inbox is a core-schema resolver, not a metadata object, so it is not part of the metadata codegen surface\").\n\n`inboxNotificationsQuery.ts` (full):\n\n```ts\nexport const INBOX_NOTIFICATIONS_QUERY = gql`\n  query InboxNotifications($includeArchived: Boolean) {\n    notifications(includeArchived: $includeArchived) {\n      id type payload createdAt readAt archivedAt\n    }\n  }\n`;\nexport type InboxNotificationsQueryResult = { notifications: InboxNotification[]; };\n```\n\n`inboxUnreadCountQuery.ts`: `query InboxUnreadCount { notificationUnreadCount }`, result `{ notificationUnreadCount: number }`.\n\n`archiveInboxNotificationsMutation.ts`: `mutation ArchiveInboxNotifications($notificationIds: [UUID!]!) { archiveNotifications(notificationIds: $notificationIds) }`.\n\n`markInboxNotificationsAsReadMutation.ts`: `mutation MarkInboxNotificationsAsRead($notificationIds: [UUID!]!) { markNotificationsAsRead(notificationIds: $notificationIds) }`.\n\n**Generated file check:** `packages/twenty-front/src/generated/graphql.ts` (1122 lines) contains **zero** notification types — grep for `Notification|notification` returned no matches. There are no generated `Not*` hooks for the inbox. This is expected because the resolver is registered with `@CoreResolver()`.\n\nServer-side schema (`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/notification/`):\n- `notification.resolver.ts:25-94` — `@CoreResolver()` with queries `notifications(includeArchived)`, `notificationUnreadCount`; mutations `markNotificationsAsRead`, `archiveNotifications`. All user/workspace-scoped from session.\n- `dtos/notification.dto.ts:10-31` — `@ObjectType('Notification')`, fields `id, type (string), payload (GraphQLJSON nullable), createdAt, readAt, archivedAt`.\n- `utils/notification-to-dto.util.ts:7-16` — entity→DTO projection.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Where the notification type enum lives (and why not on the front)\n\n**Front:** no enum/union. `InboxNotification.type: string` (types file above) and inline string literals in `InboxNotificationItem.tsx`, `filterInboxNotificationsByCategory.ts`, `resolveNotificationDeepLink.ts`.\n\n**Server (canonical):** `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/notification/constants/notification-type.constant.ts` (full, 18 lines):\n\n```ts\n// Producers emit one of these types; the value is persisted as-is in the\n// notification row and is the key a user's channel preference is looked up by.\nexport const NOTIFICATION_TYPES = [\n  'MENTION',\n  'CHAT_MESSAGE',\n  'ASSIGNED',\n  'WATCHED_RECORD_CHANGED',\n  'BUDGET_ALERT',\n  'INVOICE_OVERDUE',\n  'PAYMENT_RECEIVED',\n  'SYSTEM',\n  // P4C.4: a calendar event reminder is due (startsAt − reminderMinutes ≤ now).\n  'CALENDAR_REMINDER',\n] as const;\n\nexport type NotificationType = (typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES)[number];\n```\n\n`ObjectRecordUpdate` / `OBJECT_RECORD_UPDATE` does **not** exist in this repo (grep across `packages` returned no such identifier). The equivalent is `WATCHED_RECORD_CHANGED`.\n\nOther server constants:\n- `constants/notification-event-name.constant.ts:4` — `NOTIFICATION_REQUESTED = 'notification_requested'` (the producer event seam, consumed by `listeners/notification-requested.listener.ts`).\n- `constants/notification-channel.constant.ts`, `notification-policy.constant.ts`, `notification-watch-target-kind.constant.ts`.\n- `types/notification-request.type.ts:3-10` — `{ userId, type: NotificationType, payload, createdAt? }`.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Lingui message IDs used for notification labels\n\nAll labels use `@lingui/react/macro` `t` macros, so the **message id is the source English string itself** (no explicit `id=` / no `msg` descriptors with custom ids on the front). IDs used:\n\nIn `InboxNotificationItem.tsx`:\n- `You were mentioned` (L122), `New message` (L124), `Assigned to you` (L126), `A watched record changed` (L128), `Calendar event reminder` (L130), `An invoice is overdue` (L132), `A payment was received` (L134), `A budget threshold was reached` (L136), `System notification` (L138), `Notification` (L140)\n- `Select notification` (L192), `This notification has no destination` (L214), `Starts ${calendarReminderStartLabel}` (L219), `At the time of the event` (L181), `${calendarReminder.reminderMinutes} min before` (L182)\n\nIn `InboxFilterTabs.tsx`: `All` (L69), `Mentions` (L71), `Assigned` (L73), `Watching` (L75).\nIn `InboxBulkActions.tsx`: `${selectedCount} selected` (L59), `Mark as read` (L62), `Archive` (L65), `Clear` (L68).\nIn `InboxNotificationList.tsx`: `Today` (L69), `Yesterday` (L73), `Your inbox is empty` (L86).\nIn `InboxPage.tsx`: `Inbox` (L188), `Could not load the inbox` (L204), `Loading…` (L207).\n\n**Important:** these notification labels are **not yet present in the catalogs**. Grep of `packages/twenty-front/src/locales/generated/en.ts` and `packages/twenty-front/src/locales/en.po` for `Calendar event reminder` / `You were mentioned` / `no destination` returned **0 matches** (the generated file uses hashed ids like `\"+/y8+6\"` with English values). Tests still pass because Lingui falls back to the source message when an id is missing. Per `AGENTS.md`, do not commit catalog churn unless the task is translations.\n\nThe server email labels mirror the inbox labels but are `msg` descriptors in `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/notification/utils/notification-email-item.util.ts:15-24` (note: server uses `Calendar reminder` for `CALENDAR_REMINDER`, while the front row uses `Calendar event reminder` — a deliberate wording difference; both catalogs currently lack these strings too). `extractNotificationEmailPreview` (L32-50) uses the same preview keys `['preview','snippet','title']` as `getInboxNotificationPreview.ts:6`.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Producer / payload conventions (relevant to deep links)\n\n### Producers that exist\n\n1. **`MENTION`** — the shared mentions engine:\n   - `packages/twenty-server/src/modules/mention/services/mention-notification.service.ts:94-107` emits `type: 'MENTION'` per permitted user via `notificationService.requestNotifications`.\n   - Payload builder `packages/twenty-server/src/modules/mention/utils/build-mention-notification-payload.util.ts:7-50`:\n     - base: `{ kind: '<surface>.mention', authorId, mentionedWorkspaceMemberIds, snippet }`\n     - `chat`: `+ { channelId, messageId }`\n     - `document`: `+ { objectNameSingular: 'document', recordId: documentId, documentId }`\n     - `comment`: `+ { objectNameSingular: 'document', recordId: documentId, documentId, threadId }`\n   - `MentionSource`/`MENTION_SURFACES` at `packages/twenty-server/src/modules/mention/types/mention.type.ts:4-13`.\n   - Listeners: `modules/mention/listeners/document-mention.listener.ts`, `document-comment-mention.listener.ts`; chat via `modules/chat/services/chat-mention.service.ts` and `modules/chat/utils/chat-mention.util.ts:21-55`.\n   - Consequence: document/comment/page mentions already deep-link to `/object/document/<id>`; chat mentions to `/discussions?channelId=<id>`.\n\n2. **`CALENDAR_REMINDER`** — `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/calendar/services/calendar-reminder.service.ts:180` emits `type: 'CALENDAR_REMINDER'`; payload carries `calendarEventId`, `title`, `startsAt`, `reminderMinutes` (parsed front-side).\n\n3. **`WATCHED_RECORD_CHANGED`** — `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/notification/services/notification-watch.service.ts:205`; payload builder `utils/build-watch-notification-payload.util.ts:10-39` uses `kind: 'record.change'`, `targetKind`, and either `channelId` (CHANNEL) or `{ objectNameSingular, recordId, changedFieldNames }`.\n\n### Types with **no producer** found in `packages/twenty-server/src` (only constants/tests/email labels)\n`CHAT_MESSAGE`, `ASSIGNED`, `INVOICE_OVERDUE`, `PAYMENT_RECEIVED`, `BUDGET_ALERT`, `SYSTEM`.\n\n### No Bilan / approval producer\nGrep for `approval` / `a2e-accounting` / `bilan` in notification or producer code found nothing. `ASSIGNED` is also unproduced. So US-156 will need to add producers (and likely a new type or reuse `MENTION`/`ASSIGNED`) plus payload keys under the existing deep-link conventions.\n\n### Realtime\n- Server: `utils/notification-realtime-event.util.ts:8-59` — event `type: 'notification.inbox.updated'`, payload `{ workspaceId, userId, occurredAt, unreadCount, notifications[] }`; publisher `services/notification-realtime-publisher.service.ts`.\n- Topic builder server `utils/inbox-topic.util.ts:6-12` and front `utils/buildInboxTopic.ts:4-10` both produce `workspace:<workspaceId>:inbox:<userId>`.\n- Front event constant `INBOX_UPDATED_EVENT_TYPE = 'notification.inbox.updated'` matches the server string exactly.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Home dashboard reuse (secondary front consumer)\n\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/home-dashboard/utils/buildHomeSuggestions.ts` imports `filterInboxNotificationsByCategory`, `getInboxNotificationPreview`, and `resolveNotificationDeepLink` (L9-12). It surfaces unread mentions as `UNREAD_MENTION` suggestions (L132-146) with the same `deepLink` from `resolveNotificationDeepLink` (L74). `HomeSuggestionsWidget.tsx` uses `useInboxNotifications()` (L14). Any new notification type/deep-link behavior therefore also affects this widget.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Gaps / observations for US-156\n\n1. **No front enum** — new types are free-form strings; if you add new notification types (Bilan approval, task mention), you must add cases in `InboxNotificationItem.tsx` (label + icon), optionally in `filterInboxNotificationsByCategory.ts` (category), and ensure the payload follows one of the three deep-link conventions, otherwise the row is non-actionable (\"This notification has no destination\").\n2. **Task mentions**: no task-surface mention path currently. `MentionSource` only has `chat | document | comment` (mention.type.ts:10-13). Adding `task` requires extending `MentionSource`, `MENTION_SURFACES`, `buildMentionNotificationPayload` (payload should carry `{ objectNameSingular: 'task', recordId }` to deep-link to `/object/task/<id>`).\n3. **Page mentions** already resolve to `/object/document/<id>` (not `/bureau`). If US-156 wants Bureau routes, `resolveNotificationDeepLink` would need a document-specific branch before the generic record branch.\n4. **Bilan approvals**: no producer and no approvable entity mapping exists; the inbox would need a new notification type or reuse `ASSIGNED`/`SYSTEM`, plus a payload carrying `{ objectNameSingular, recordId }` (or a dedicated route).\n5. **`filterInboxNotificationsByCategory` maps only 3 types**; unrecognized types appear only in the `all` tab.\n6. **The categories are fixed to `all | mentions | assigned | watching`** (`InboxNotificationCategory`), so adding an \"Approvals\" tab is a type + UI change.\n7. **`resolveNotificationDeepLink` is the single source of truth** used by both `InboxPage.handleOpenNotification` and `buildHomeSuggestions`, so extending it propagates to both surfaces.\n8. **No generated GraphQL for notifications** — any new fields/DTO changes are server-side core schema + hand-written front `gql` documents; do not expect codegen to produce types.\n</task_result>\n</task>",
