        "result": "<task id=\"ses_f06839014ffegHA9tAUc44O1TA\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nI have completed a thorough exploration. Here is the full research report.\n\n---\n\n# A2E Suite — Document mention index (US-139/M8d), a2e-documents, mention paths & Bilan approvals\n\n## 1. The document mention index (`packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-documents/src/lib/document-mentions.ts`)\n\nFull file is 345 lines. It is the **M8d save-time mention index (US-139)**: a writer (`syncDocumentMentions`) run once per document save, and a reader (`listMentionedInDocuments`) run per record-page view. It never selects document `content` on read.\n\n### Constants (lines 18–25)\n```ts\nexport const MENTION_INLINE_CONTENT_TYPE = 'mention';\nexport const MENTION_INDEX_PAGE_SIZE = 500;   // one document's outgoing mentions\nexport const MENTIONED_IN_PAGE_SIZE = 200;    // a record's incoming backlinks\n```\n\n### Types (lines 35–76)\n```ts\nexport type DocumentMentionTarget = {\n  objectNameSingular: string;\n  recordId: string;\n  label: string | null;\n};\n\nexport type DocumentMentionIndexRow = {\n  mentionKey: string;\n  documentId: string;\n  targetObjectNameSingular: string;\n  targetRecordId: string;\n  targetLabel: string | null;\n};\n\nexport type ExistingDocumentMentionRow = {\n  id: string;\n  mentionKey: string;\n  targetLabel: string | null;\n};\n\nexport type MentionIndexDiff = {\n  toCreate: DocumentMentionIndexRow[];\n  toDelete: ExistingDocumentMentionRow[];\n  toUpdate: { id: string; targetLabel: string | null }[];\n};\n\nexport type MentionIndexSyncResult = {\n  created: number; deleted: number; updated: number;\n};\n\nexport type MentionedInTarget = { objectNameSingular: string; recordId: string; };\n\nexport type MentionedInDocument = {\n  documentId: string; title: string; isArchived: boolean;\n};\n```\n\n### `mentionKey` format (lines 81–85)\n```ts\nexport const buildMentionKey = (\n  documentId: string,\n  target: Pick<DocumentMentionTarget, 'objectNameSingular' | 'recordId'>,\n): string => `${documentId}:${target.objectNameSingular}:${target.recordId}`;\n```\nSo a key is `\"<documentId>:<objectNameSingular>:<recordId>\"`, e.g. `document-1:task:task-1`. Test asserts exactly this (`document-mentions.test.ts:139`).\n\n### Mention node extraction (`extractDocumentMentionTargets`, lines 94–157)\nStructural walk of the serialized BlockNote tree. Any object whose `type === 'mention'` is a hit; reads `props.objectNameSingular`, `props.recordId`, optional `props.label`. Requires both `objectNameSingular` and `recordId` as non-empty strings; otherwise the node is skipped (legacy `objectMetadataId`-only shape skipped, `:135`). Dedupes by `${objectNameSingular}:${recordId}`. Malformed JSON / empty → `[]` (`:97-107`). Recurses arrays and all object values (`:112-152`).\n\nThe mention node shape it reads is defined in the front editor: `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/blocknote-editor/blocks/MentionInlineContent.tsx:84-105` — `type: 'mention'`, props `{ recordId, objectMetadataId, objectNameSingular, label, imageUrl }`, `content: 'none'`.\n\n### `buildMentionIndexRows` (lines 159–169)\nMaps targets into index rows, injecting `documentId` + `mentionKey`.\n\n### `diffMentionIndex` (lines 174–198)\nDelta only: `toCreate` = desired not in existing; `toDelete` = existing not in desired; `toUpdate` = label changed. Keeps row ids for updates.\n\n### `syncDocumentMentions` — the writer (lines 200–273)\n- Client type: `DocumentMentionsClient = Pick<CoreApiClient, 'query' | 'mutation'>`.\n- Reads existing rows via `query { documentMentions(filter: { document: { id: { eq: documentId } } }, first: 500) { edges { node { id mentionKey targetLabel } } } }` (`:211-228`).\n- Applies diff: bulk `createDocumentMentions` (`:245-250`), per-row `deleteDocumentMention` (`:253-257`), per-row `updateDocumentMention` (`:259-266`).\n- Returns `{ created, deleted, updated }`.\n\n### `listMentionedInDocuments` — the reader (lines 290–345)\n- Client: `MentionedInClient = Pick<CoreApiClient, 'query'>`.\n- Guards empty target → `[]` without a query (`:300-302`).\n- Query:\n```ts\ndocumentMentions: {\n  __args: {\n    filter: {\n      targetObjectNameSingular: { eq: target.objectNameSingular },\n      targetRecordId: { eq: target.recordId },\n    },\n    first: MENTIONED_IN_PAGE_SIZE, // 200\n  },\n  edges: { node: { id: true, document: { id: true, title: true, archivedAt: true } } },\n}\n```\n- Resolves each edge's `document` relation; drops null relations (unreadable docs) and null ids (`:324-333`), dedupes by document id (`:331`), `isArchived` = `archivedAt` non-empty (`:338`), sorts by title (`:342-344`). **Never selects `content`.**\n\n### Who calls the reader?\nImportant: `listMentionedInDocuments` is currently **not imported anywhere in application code** — only in `src/lib/__tests__/document-mentions.test.ts`. The \"Mentioned in\" UI/tab/widget (the remaining M8d bullet) is **not yet mounted**. `document-mentions.ts` imports only `CoreApiClient` type; the module is pure/testable.\n\n### Tests\n`src/lib/__tests__/document-mentions.test.ts` (415 lines) covers extraction (nested blocks, dedupe, legacy skip, malformed), key stability, save create/delete/update/no-op, label refresh, read model (no content, unreadable drop, dedupe, invalid target no-query), and diff.\n\n---\n\n## 2. The `documentMention` object and the DB-event logic function\n\n### `src/objects/document-mention.object.ts` (87 lines)\n`defineObject` with `universalIdentifier: OBJECT_IDS.documentMention` (`c31a0500-0000-4000-8000-000000000000`), `nameSingular: 'documentMention'`, `namePlural: 'documentMentions'`, label `Mention de document`, icon `IconAt`, label identifier = `mentionKey`.\n\nFields (lines 35–86):\n| name | type | notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `mentionKey` | TEXT, unique | label id `c31a0500-0001-...0001`; stable `${documentId}:${objectNameSingular}:${recordId}` |\n| `targetObjectNameSingular` | TEXT | `c31a0500-0001-...0002` |\n| `targetRecordId` | TEXT | `c31a0500-0001-...0003` |\n| `targetLabel` | TEXT, nullable | `c31a0500-0001-...0004` |\n| `document` | RELATION manyToOne → `document`, join column `documentId`, `onDelete: CASCADE` | `RELATION_IDS.documentMentionDocument` / inverse `documentMentions` |\n\nDesign note (lines 10–23): target is **polymorphic by design** (object-name + record-id pair, no relation), because the index only reads it back as a filter. Rows hang off the document by FK, so deleting a document cascades the index and permissions inherit.\n\n### `src/logic-functions/index-document-mentions.ts` (76 lines)\n- Imports `CoreApiClient`, `defineLogicFunction`, `DatabaseEventPayload`; `readDocumentRevisionBody`/`DocumentRevisionCasRecord` from `../lib/document-revision-cas.ts` (line 9–11), `syncDocumentMentions` (line 12).\n- Event payload type (lines 24–31): `DatabaseEventPayload<{ recordId: string; properties: { before?, after?, updatedFields? } }>`.\n- `handler` (lines 33–63):\n  - `recordId` undefined → `{ skipped: 'no-record' }`.\n  - If `updatedFields` defined and missing `'content'` → `{ skipped: 'content-unchanged' }` (defensive; prevents wiping index).\n  - `after` missing → `{ skipped: 'no-after' }`.\n  - `new CoreApiClient()`; `syncDocumentMentions(client, recordId, readDocumentRevisionBody(after.content))`; returns `{ indexed: result }`.\n- `defineLogicFunction` (lines 65–75):\n```ts\nexport default defineLogicFunction({\n  universalIdentifier: LOGIC_FUNCTION_IDS.indexDocumentMentions, // c31a0000-0012-...000b\n  name: 'index-document-mentions',\n  description: '…',\n  timeoutSeconds: 60,\n  databaseEventTriggerSettings: {\n    eventName: 'document.updated',\n    updatedFields: ['content'],\n  },\n  handler,\n});\n```\nComment (lines 14–22) notes the app SDK exposes only **post-commit** database events, so the index is reconciled here, and `document.updated` has three independent subscribers: this, `guard-document-parent-cycle`, `guard-document-revision-save`.\n\n### Registration / IDs\n- Object id and relation ids in `src/constants/universal-identifiers.ts:19` and `:36-37`.\n- Logic function id `indexDocumentMentions: 'c31a0000-0012-4000-8000-00000000000b'` (`:83`). Comment (`:81-82`) confirms M8d.\n- Built manifest entry: `.twenty/output/manifest.json:830-845` (name, desc, `databaseEventTriggerSettings` `document.updated` / `[\"content\"]`, source/built paths).\n- Document side relation: `src/objects/document.object.ts:207-218` (`mentions` O2M → `documentMention`).\n- Page layout has no mention widget yet: `src/page-layouts/document.page-layout.ts` has FIELDS + FIELD_RICH_TEXT + `documentPage` FRONT_COMPONENT + Timeline only.\n\n---\n\n## 3. How a2e-documents declares apps/objects/logic functions/triggers\n\n### App config\n`src/application.config.ts` (11 lines):\n```ts\nexport const APPLICATION_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIER = '19126a9c-7cc0-4368-aaba-c7e5a87b0c48';\nexport default defineApplication({ universalIdentifier, displayName: 'Bureau', description: '…' });\n```\n\n### package.json (`a2e-documents/package.json:1-32`)\n- `\"name\": \"a2e-documents\"`, version `0.2.12`, `engines.twenty: \">=2.19.0\"`.\n- devDeps: `twenty-client-sdk@2.31.0`, `twenty-sdk@2.31.0`, TS 5.9, oxlint, React 19.\n- scripts: `twenty`, `lint` (oxlint), `typecheck` (tsc --noEmit), `test:unit` (node --test with `src/lib/__tests__/*.test.ts` and `src/logic-functions/__tests__/*.test.ts`).\n\n### File-declaration pattern\nEach declarable thing is a default-exported `defineX` in a directory:\n- `src/objects/*.object.ts` → `defineObject`\n- `src/fields/*.field.ts` → `defineField`\n- `src/logic-functions/*.ts` (some `.logic-function.ts`) → `defineLogicFunction`\n- `src/front-components/*.front-component.tsx` → `defineFrontComponent`\n- `src/page-layouts/*.page-layout.ts` → `definePageLayout`\n- `src/views/*.view.ts`, `src/navigation-menu-items/*`, `src/command-menu-items/*`, `src/roles/*`\n\nThe `twenty` CLI builds these into `.twenty/output/manifest.json` (verified; `logicFunctions` array at manifest line 630, `frontComponents` at 847), and compiles handlers to `.mjs`. Universal identifiers are committed forever in `constants/universal-identifiers.ts` (namespace documented at lines 1–12; family codes `0000 object … 0012 logic function`).\n\n### `defineLogicFunction` trigger variants present in a2e-documents\n- `databaseEventTriggerSettings: { eventName: 'document.updated', updatedFields: [...] }` — `guard-document-parent-cycle.ts:81-84`, `guard-document-revision-save.ts` (manifest 707-712), `index-document-mentions.ts:71-74`.\n- `cronTriggerSettings: { pattern: '0 4 * * *' }` — `purge-archived-documents.ts` (manifest 647-649).\n- `toolTriggerSettings: { inputSchema }` (AI tool) — `document-content.logic-function.ts:34-52`, `summarize-document`, `translate-document`, `improve-document-writing`.\n- Plain (no trigger) — `post-install`, `list-template-descriptors`, `apply-template`.\n\n### `CoreApiClient` usage pattern\nImported from `twenty-client-sdk/core`, constructed inside the handler:\n```ts\nimport { CoreApiClient } from 'twenty-client-sdk/core';\nconst client = new CoreApiClient();\nawait client.query({ documents: { __args: {...}, edges: { node: {...} } } } as never);\nawait client.mutation({ updateDocument: { __args: { id, data }, id: true } } as never);\n```\nSee `guard-document-parent-cycle.ts:1,40,47-70`; `index-document-mentions.ts:1,55`; `front-components/create-document-command.front-component.tsx:1,25-39`.\n\n### `defineFrontComponent` pattern\n`create-document-command.front-component.tsx:60-66`:\n```ts\nexport default defineFrontComponent({\n  universalIdentifier: CREATE_DOCUMENT_COMMAND_FRONT_COMPONENT_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIER,\n  name: 'create-document-command',\n  description: '…',\n  component: CreateDocumentCommand,\n});\n```\nFront components import `Command`, `AppPath`, `navigate` from `twenty-sdk/front-component` and `CoreApiClient` from `twenty-client-sdk/core`.\n\n### Front-component widget mount in a page layout\n`document.page-layout.ts:37-45` — widget `type: 'FRONT_COMPONENT'`, `configuration: { configurationType: 'FRONT_COMPONENT', frontComponentUniversalIdentifier: FRONT_COMPONENT_IDS.documentPage }`. (Same pattern `a2e-links` uses for its Related tab, see phase-15-report:35.)\n\n---\n\n## 4. Existing mention paths (chat / document / comment / task)\n\n### 4a. The server-side shared mentions engine — `packages/twenty-server/src/modules/mention/**`\nThis is the P8.2 \"mentions engine\", already built and green (PLAN.md:2261-2264). It produces `MENTION` notification requests.\n\n- **Types** `types/mention.type.ts`: `MENTION_SURFACES = ['document','chat','comment']`; `MentionSource`:\n  - chat → `{ surface:'chat'; channelId; messageId }`\n  - document → `{ surface:'document'; documentId }`\n  - comment → `{ surface:'comment'; documentId; threadId }`\n  - `MentionTarget = { workspaceMemberId; userId }`; `MentionExtraction = { mentionedWorkspaceMemberIds; contextSnippet }`.\n- **Dispatcher** `utils/parse-mentions.util.ts:18-35` → `parseChatMentions` / `parseDocumentMentions` / comment thread.\n- **BlockNote parser** `utils/parse-blocknote-mentions.util.ts`: walks `type:'mention'` inline nodes exactly like the app-side extractor; **only `objectNameSingular === 'workspaceMember'` produces notifications** (`:76-84`); record mentions only contribute their `@label` to the context text (`:86-91`). Also handles comment entry projection and new-comment selection (`:168-215`).\n- **Chat parser** `utils/parse-chat-mentions.util.ts` (Markdown-lite).\n- **Notification producer** `services/mention-notification.service.ts`:\n  - `notifyMentions(...)` (`:44-110`): parse → subtract previously-mentioned (`excludeWorkspaceMemberIds`) → resolve member→user (`:115-144`, workspace ORM, bypass permission) → `filterPermittedMentionTargets` via `MentionAccessService` → `notificationService.requestNotifications({ requests: [{ userId, type:'MENTION', payload }] })`.\n- **Permission** `services/mention-access.service.ts`: reuses `RealtimeTopicAccessService.canWorkspaceMemberReadChatChannel` / `canWorkspaceMemberReadObjectRecord`; unreadable target → suppressed.\n- **Payload** `utils/build-mention-notification-payload.util.ts`: base `{ kind: '<surface>.mention', authorId, mentionedWorkspaceMemberIds, snippet }`; chat adds `channelId`/`messageId`; document adds `objectNameSingular:'document'`, `recordId`, `documentId`; comment adds the same + `threadId`.\n- **Listeners**:\n  - `listeners/document-mention.listener.ts` — `@OnDatabaseBatchEvent('document', CREATED|UPDATED)`, filters `updatedFields.includes('content')`, diff-subtracts mentions present in `before.content`, source `{ surface:'document', documentId }`.\n  - `listeners/document-comment-mention.listener.ts` — `@OnDatabaseBatchEvent('documentCommentThread', CREATED|UPDATED)`, filters `updatedFields.includes('comments')`, notifies only newly added comments, source `{ surface:'comment', documentId, threadId }`.\n  - `listeners/chat-mention.listener.ts` — `@OnDatabaseBatchEvent('chatMessage', CREATED)` (edits do not re-notify).\n- **Module** `mention.module.ts`; registered from `core-engine.module.ts` (per phase-08-report:53).\n\n### 4b. Chat mention path\n- **Wire format**: `a2e-chat/src/lib/message-body.ts:1-28` — body is plain text; mentions encoded `@[label](workspaceMemberId)`; `MENTION_PATTERN = /@\\[[^\\]]*\\]\\(([^)\\s]+)\\)/g`; `extractMentionedWorkspaceMemberIds` (`:15-27`). Note: this extractor is **only referenced by its own test** in the app; the server engine re-implements/parses it.\n- **Chat object**: `a2e-chat/src/objects/chat-message.object.ts` — `body` (TEXT), `editedAt`, relations `channel`, `author`, `threadParent`/`threadReplies`, `reactions`, `readCursors`. No mention index/field.\n- **Read cursor**: `a2e-chat/src/objects/chat-read-cursor.object.ts` — per (channel, member) `lastReadAt`, `lastReadMessage`.\n- **Server chat path**: `chat/listeners/chat-mention.listener.ts` → `chat/services/chat-mention.service.ts:16-34` maps the message to `{ surface:'chat', channelId, messageId }` and calls the shared engine.\n- **Front composer**: `twenty-front/src/modules/chat/utils/chatMentionDraft.ts` (`buildChatMentionMarkup` `@[label](id)`, `insertChatMentionIntoDraft`); `ChatComposer.tsx:105-174` autocomplete via `useChatMentionCandidates.ts` → `@/mention/hooks/useMentionSearch.ts` (core `SEARCH_QUERY`, filtered to readable+active+searchable non-system objects). Rendering: `ChatMessageBody.tsx` → `splitChatMessageBody.ts` (`MENTION_PATTERN`).\n- **Front inbox producer contract**: chat payload `kind:'chat.mention'` deep-links via `channelId` (see `resolveNotificationDeepLink.ts:47-51`).\n\n### 4c. Shared front mention module (`twenty-front/src/modules/mention/**`)\n`MentionChip`, `MentionRecordChip`, `MentionMenuListItem`, `MentionSuggestionMenu`, `MentionSuggestion.ts`, `MentionTag.ts`, `useMentionMenu.ts`, `useMentionSearch.ts`, `MentionSearchResult.ts`. `MentionSearchResult = { recordId, objectNameSingular, objectLabelSingular, label, imageUrl }`. This is the record-mention picker reused by BlockNote and chat.\n\n### 4d. Task mention paths\nThere is **no task-mention path**. Grep for `mention` across `a2e-projects/src` returned **nothing**. The server has no task mention code (`grep task.*mention` in `packages/twenty-server/src/modules` → empty). Tasks get notifications only through:\n- **Assignment** (`ASSIGNED` notification type exists at `notification-type.constant.ts:6`), and\n- **Watching** (`notification-watch.listener.ts:70-75` `task` UPDATED → `WATCHED_RECORD_CHANGED`).\n- `a2e-projects` has no notification logic; its `task-due-reminder.logic-function.ts:18` explicitly says it uses the calendar's native reminder primitive, \"no second notification engine\".\n\n### 4e. Inbox / notification core (P8)\n- **NotificationService** `engine/core-modules/notification/services/notification.service.ts`: `requestNotifications({ workspaceId, requests })` emits `NOTIFICATION_REQUESTED` custom batch event (`:47-59`); `dispatchNotifications` applies per-user channel preference + quiet hours (`:61-139`); `findForUser`, `countUnread`, `markAsRead`, `archiveNotifications` (`:176-273`).\n- **Types** `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` (`constants/notification-type.constant.ts:3-16`): `MENTION`, `CHAT_MESSAGE`, `ASSIGNED`, `WATCHED_RECORD_CHANGED`, `BUDGET_ALERT`, `INVOICE_OVERDUE`, `PAYMENT_RECEIVED`, `SYSTEM`, `CALENDAR_REMINDER`.\n- **Listener** `listeners/notification-requested.listener.ts` → dispatch → realtime publish on `workspace:<id>:inbox:<userId>` + email digest.\n- **Watchers** `listeners/notification-watch.listener.ts` (document/note/task/opportunity/company/person/channel); `services/notification-watch.service.ts` (`notifyWatchersOfChange`), payload `utils/build-watch-notification-payload.util.ts` (`kind:'record.change'`, `objectNameSingular`, `recordId` or `channelId`).\n- **Front inbox** `twenty-front/src/modules/inbox/**`: `InboxNotification.ts` (categories `all|mentions|assigned|watching`), `filterInboxNotificationsByCategory.ts` maps `mentions → ['MENTION']`, `resolveNotificationDeepLink.ts` (calendar reminder / chat / `{objectNameSingular, recordId}`), `getInboxNotificationPreview.ts` (keys `preview|snippet|title`), hooks `useInboxNotifications`/`useInboxUnreadCount`/`useInboxBulkActions`/`useInboxLive`, page route `/inbox`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Bilan / a2e-accounting approval events\n\n### Objects with approval/status\n- **`fiche.object.ts`** (the official document object):\n  - `status` SELECT (`:118-155`): `DRAFT` (Brouillon), `SUBMITTED` (Déposée), **`APPROVED` (Validée)**, `ARCHIVED` (Archivée).\n  - `submittedAt` DATE_TIME (`:216-222`), **`approvedAt` DATE_TIME (`:224-230`, \"Validée le\")**.\n  - Ids: `field-identifiers.ts:136` (`approvedAt: 'b11a0900-0001-...000b'`).\n- **`invoice.object.ts`** `status` (`:48-52`): `DRAFT`, `SENT`, `PARTIALLY_PAID`, `PAID`, `OVERDUE`, `CANCELLED` (`field-vocabulary.ts:110-124`).\n- **`quote.object.ts`** `status` (`:45-49`): `DRAFT`, `SENT`, `ACCEPTED`, `REFUSED`, `EXPIRED`, `CONVERTED` (`field-vocabulary.ts:126-140`).\n- `savedSubvention` has `status` including `GRANTED` (used by `grant-subvention-income.ts:40`).\n\n### Is there an approval workflow / event / notification path?\n**No dedicated approval event, workflow, notification, or object exists.**\n- `grep -iE \"approval|approve|validation|statut|validate\"` over `a2e-accounting/src` only found: field labels (`Statut`), the `APPROVED` option + `approvedAt` field, fiche template text, and unrelated validation/tests. There is **no `approval` object, no `*approval*` file, no logic function on `fiche.status`/`fiche.approvedAt`**.\n- The only DB-event-triggered accounting logic functions are:\n  - `sync-invoice-to-ledger.ts:72-73` → `eventName: 'invoice.*'`\n  - `stamp-invoice-number.ts:43-44` → `eventName: 'invoice.*'`\n  - `sync-finance-entry-to-ledger.ts:88-89` → `eventName: 'financeEntry.*'`\n  - `grant-subvention-income.ts:86-89` → `eventName: 'savedSubvention.updated'`, `updatedFields: ['status','amountGranted','decisionAt']` (the closest thing to a status-driven \"approved\" flow — it books income when `status === 'GRANTED'`, `:40`).\n  - Cron: `generate-recurring-documents.ts:139`, `rollup-budgets.ts:137`, `refresh-subventions.ts:14`, `sweep-overdue-invoices.ts:54`.\n- `a2e-accounting/README.md` has no approval/notification workflow. `LOGIC_FUNCTION_IDS` (`universal-identifiers.ts:98-115`) contains no approval/render-fiche implementation file (id `renderFiche` is declared but no `render-fiche.ts` file exists).\n- Accounting objects **do** get `WATCHED_RECORD_CHANGED` only for standard objects listed in `notification-watch.listener.ts`; `fiche`/`invoice`/`quote` are app objects and are **not** in that list, so they have no watch notifications either.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Synthesis for US-156 (unified inbox notifications for mentions)\n\n### Task definition\n- **PLAN.md:561-562 — M11e \"Unified activity & inbox.\"** \"Mentions from pages, chat, tasks, Bilan approvals flow into the native Inbox (P8) with deep links.\" Still `[ ]`.\n- **PLAN.md:367-369 — M8d** \"Mentioned in\" panel still `[ ]`.\n- `docs/plan/phases/phase-15-report.md:128-140` (US-155/M11d): the intended US-156 mechanism is the **cross-app events contract (`cross_app_lifecycle`)**; the pre-existing notification path (`NOTIFICATION_REQUESTED`/`NotificationWatchListener`) \"will subscribe to `cross_app_lifecycle` for US-156\"; next action is \"US-156 subscribes `@OnEvent(CROSS_APP_LIFECYCLE_EVENT)`\".\n\n### The C5 cross-app event infrastructure (US-155/M11d, already built)\n- Constant: `packages/twenty-server/src/modules/cross-app-events/constants/cross-app-lifecycle-event.constant.ts` → `CROSS_APP_LIFECYCLE_EVENT = 'cross_app_lifecycle'`.\n- Wildcard listener: `listeners/cross-app-lifecycle-event.listener.ts` (`@OnDatabaseBatchEvent('*', …)` for the 6 actions) → `services/cross-app-event-emitter.service.ts` (gates on `resolveCrossAppEventObjectFamily`, checks `flatApplicationMaps` install state, `workspaceEventEmitter.emitCustomBatchEvent(CROSS_APP_LIFECYCLE_EVENT, …, workspaceId)`).\n- Pure projector: `utils/map-database-event-to-cross-app-events.util.ts` (maps DB action→contract action, promotes `task` → `completed`, resolves actor/timestamps, returns `CrossAppEventPayload[]`).\n- Shared contract + vocabulary: `packages/twenty-shared/src/cross-app-events/**` (`buildCrossAppEventPayload`, `computeCrossAppEventName`, `resolveCrossAppEventObjectFamily`, `CROSS_APP_EVENT_ACTIVATION_APP_BY_FAMILY`, family/action/actor/payload/name types).\n- Not yet consumed by any notification/inbox subscriber at HEAD.\n\n### Key gaps relevant to US-156\n1. **M8d mention index is not wired to notifications.** `documentMention` rows are created at save time, but nothing turns them into `MENTION` notifications. The server `DocumentMentionListener` independently re-parses the document body for **workspaceMember** mentions only (`parse-blocknote-mentions.util.ts:76-91`) — **record mentions (task, company, etc.) produce no notification**. The M8d index captures record targets but only for the \"Mentioned in\" backlink reader, and that reader is not mounted anywhere.\n2. **No task mention path.** Tasks only have `ASSIGNED` and `WATCHED_RECORD_CHANGED`.\n3. **No Bilan approval event/notification.** `fiche.status=APPROVED` / `approvedAt` are inert fields; no listener, workflow, or notification type.\n4. **The inbox front and notification core are complete** (`MENTION` type, `mentions` tab filter, deep-link resolver, realtime, preferences) — US-156 should extend these seams, not create a parallel system (C5).\n5. **Deep-link payload conventions**: existing producers use `{ kind, snippet, objectNameSingular, recordId }` for records/docs and `{ channelId, messageId }` for chat; `resolveNotificationDeepLink` handles both, plus `CALENDAR_REMINDER` via `calendarEventId`. `getInboxNotificationPreview` reads `preview|snippet|title`.\n6. **The M8d reader contract** (`listMentionedInDocuments`) is the only app-side read model; if US-156 routes through it, it accepts a polymorphic `{ objectNameSingular, recordId }` target, matching the cross-app payload shape.\n\n### Most relevant files to touch/consult for US-156\n- Server producer seam: `engine/core-modules/notification/services/notification.service.ts:47` (`requestNotifications`), `.../listeners/notification-watch.listener.ts`, `.../services/notification-watch.service.ts:144`.\n- Permission primitives: `modules/mention/services/mention-access.service.ts`, `realtime-gateway/services/realtime-topic-access.service.ts`.\n- C5 channel: `modules/cross-app-events/**`.\n- App index/writer: `a2e-documents/src/lib/document-mentions.ts`, `.../objects/document-mention.object.ts`, `.../logic-functions/index-document-mentions.ts`.\n- Front inbox: `twenty-front/src/modules/inbox/**`, `twenty-front/src/modules/mention/**`, `twenty-front/src/modules/chat/**`.\n- Docs: `PLAN.md:561-562`, `docs/plan/phases/phase-15-report.md:128-140`, `docs/plan/phases/phase-08-report.md:49-58` (mentions engine report).\n\nNo code was written or modified; this is research only.\n</task_result>\n</task>"
